//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
//
// Documentation for Kitsune-specific attributes. This is used to generate an
// HTML page with the documentation.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

// This is named GlobalDocumentationOverride because an entity named
// GlobalDocumentation will be found in clang/Basic/KitsuneAttrDocs.td. That
// file includes clang/Basic/Attr.td which includes clang/Basic/AttrDocs.td.
// AttrDocs.td contains a definition of GlobalDocumentation.
//
// clang-tblgen has been modified so the -gen-kitsune-attr-docs action expects
// GlobalDocumentationOverride.
//
// Yes, this is a really lousy workaround, but clang's attribute organization
// is somewhat awkward. While it is is fixable, it would make it harder to keep
// it sync'ed with upstream. Any changes that we make are unlikely to be
// accepted upstream, so this will have to do.
//
def GlobalDocumentationOverride {
  code Intro =[{..
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  NOTE: This file is automatically generated by running clang-tblgen
  -gen-kitsune-attr-docs. Do not edit this file by hand!!
  -------------------------------------------------------------------

====================================
Kitsune Attributes
====================================
.. contents::
   :local:

.. |br| raw:: html

  <br/>

Introduction
============

These are attributes that are currently supported in Kitsune. They may be
accepted by `Clang <https://clang.llvm.org>`__, but will have no effect there.

.. warning::

  Many of these are experimental and primarily intended for use by Kitsune's
  developers. While we try to keep the documentation here consistent with the
  implementation, there is a good chance that the actual behavior will differ
  significantly from the documentation.

}];
}

#define GENERATING_DOCS
include "clang/Basic/Attr.td"
